{
  "title": "Anterolateral Bowing & Congenital Pseudoarthrosis of Tibia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4056/anterolateral-bowing-and-congenital-pseudoarthrosis-of-tibia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 5 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anterolateral Bowing and Congenital Pseudoarthrosis of the Tibia are congenital conditions, most commonly associated with Neurofibromatosis Type 1, that present with a bowing deformity of the tibial.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is confirmed with radiographs of the tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with bracing for patients who are weightbearing without pseudoarthrosis or fracture. Surgical correction is indicated in the presence of pseudoarthrosis or fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Extremely rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "1:140,000-190,000",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk Factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Up to 55% associated with Neurofibromatosis Type 1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "15% associated with Fibrous Dysplasia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pseudoarthrosis in not congenital, but in fact develops post-natally due to fracture non-union",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Three types of tibial bowing exist in children",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**anterolateral bowing (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**posteromedial bowing (physiologic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anteromedial bowing (fibular hemimelia)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anterolateral bowing is a continuum of disease that can be divided into",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**anterolateral bowing of tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4056/images/tibial%20bowing%20xray%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**congenital pseudarthrosis of tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4056/images/Congenital%20pseudo%20xray%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**neurofibromatosis type I**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "is found in 50-55% of patients with anterolateral bowing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "only 6-10% of patients with neurofibromatosis will have anterolateral tibial bowing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Numerous classification systems have been proposed (Boyd, Andersen, Crawford) however none guide management or are predictive of outcome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Two classification criteria have been proposed to guide treatment:**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The presence or absence of fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "The age at which fracture occurs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Early onset\" < 4 years old",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "\"Late onset\" > 4 years old",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "majority present with bowing in the first year of life",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "careful skin examination for cafe-au-lait spots and other signs of neurofibromatosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The lesion does not self-resolve, and once fracture occurs there is low likelihood of spontaneous resolution",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bracing in clamshell orthosis or patellar tendon bearing (PTB) orthosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "children of ambulatory age (weight bearing)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bowing without pseudarthrosis or fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "spontaneous remodeling is not expected",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "goal is to prevent further bowing and fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "osteotomy for bowing alone is contraindicated",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "maintained until skeletal maturity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bowing with **pseudarthrosis or fracture**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "amputation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "typically indicated after multiple failed surgical attempts at union",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "severe limb length discrepancy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "dysfunctional angular deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Method- Syme or Boyd amputation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Surgical fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "goals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "resection of pseudarthrosis to grossly normal bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "correction of alignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bone grafting and stabilization of the remaining segments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "intramedullary splinting of the bone is desired",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "techniques",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intramedullary nailing with bone grafting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4056/images/indianjorthop_2012_46_6_616_104184_f3.jpg",
                      "caption": "shows nailing of anterolateral bowing"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Resect the pseudarthrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Tibial shortening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Fixation with intramedullary rod",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Bone graft",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "free vascularized fibular graft (Farmer's Procedure)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4056/images/Free%20fibula%20graft%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "contralateral fibula is used, ipsilateral is involved in pseudarthrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Ilizarov or circular frame fixation with lengthening or bone transport",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Amputation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Ankle disarticulation (Boyd or Syme amputation) preferred over resection at pseudoarthrosis site",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Persistent motion at pseudoarthrosis site managed by prosthetic socket",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrent fracture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen in 50% or more of patients even after initial union",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Valgus deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Limb length discrepancy at skeletal maturity (average 5cm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "No treatment is considered to produce results in a predictable and acceptable fashion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
